{"name":"Blue Spruce","hex":"#adc5c9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue spruce","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spruce tree of species Picea pungens, native to the Rocky Mountains of North America, often planted as an ornamental."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_spruce"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue spruce","blocks":[{"text":"The blue spruce, also commonly known as Colorado spruce or Colorado blue spruce, is a species of spruce tree native to North America in Arizona, Colorado, Idaho, New Mexico, Utah and Wyoming. It is noted for its often strongly glaucous blue-green needles, and has therefore been used as an ornamental tree in many places far beyond its native range."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Blue_Spruce_%2815905530369%29.jpg/330px-Blue_Spruce_%2815905530369%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_spruce"},{"title":"Spruce","blocks":[{"text":"A spruce is a tree of the genus Picea, a genus of some 37 species of coniferous trees in the pine family, Pinaceae, found in the northern temperate and boreal (taiga) regions of the Northern Hemisphere. Picea is treated either in the subfamily Pinoideae, or the sole genus in its own subfamily Piceoideae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Picea_abies.jpg/330px-Picea_abies.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spruce"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an 